**Findings**
1. **[P2] Python/TS do not cover the legacy readable-but-not-reapplicable case.**  
   Rust pins this in [slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:421](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:421): raw legacy row reads back, re-apply raises `WriteValidation`, adding `Searchable` remedies it. Python and TS only assert new rejection/control at [test_slice15d_projection_registry.py:418](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/python/tests/test_slice15d_projection_registry.py:418) and [slice15d-projection-registry.test.ts:571](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/ts/tests/slice15d-projection-registry.test.ts:571). They do not seed a legacy registry row and assert `read.projections` behavior. This is under-covering for item 5.

2. **[P3] `deferred_only_mutation_is_reported_not_unchanged` no longer tests the “unchanged lie” half.**  
   In [slice15d_projection_registry.rs:1288](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice15d_projection_registry.rs:1288), the promoted spec is `rankable + searchable + vector`. Because `searchable` makes `desired.wants_eav()` true, the changed branch pushes `delta.built` at [lib.rs:17543](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17543). So `assert!(!second.unchanged)` would pass even with the old bad guard. The test still catches the exact old guard through `second.deferred.contains(...)`, but the name and primary “deferred-only” framing are now misleading.

**Numbered Review**
1. `deferred_only_mutation_is_reported_not_unchanged`:  
   a. Not vacuous. Against the pre-fix guard `desired.has_deferred() && !existing.has_deferred()`, the rerouted test would still fail because the raw update makes `existing.has_deferred() == true`, so old code would suppress `delta.deferred`; the test asserts `second.deferred.contains("importance")` at [slice15d_projection_registry.rs:1346](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice15d_projection_registry.rs:1346).  
   b. Yes, it is no longer deferred-only. `searchable` makes EAV build, so the `unchanged=false` oracle is weakened/non-load-bearing.  
   c. The doc-comment’s unconstructible claim is true for public Rust specs: pure deferred-only means no `filterable`/`searchable`, so any mutation must be in `fts`/`vector`, and [lib.rs:17486](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17486) rejects that without `searchable`.

2. TC-71 runtime gate: no defect found. `vector_projection_declared` remains role-aware at [lib.rs:17910](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17910), and reconciliation remains reachable on boot and configure via [lib.rs:17842](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17842) and [lib.rs:17577](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17577). Tests cover forward, late-write, inverse, boot, and configure reconciliation. Raw seeding matches `persist_projection_row` storage at [lib.rs:17084](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17084).

3. Reject loop placement: no request-partial-apply defect found. Shape validation runs before `vector_declared_before`, drops, load/diff, and backfill in `apply_projection_config` at [lib.rs:17486](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17486). Mixed valid+invalid+drop total no-op is tested at [slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:283](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:283). Caveat: public `configure_projections` drains pre-existing async work before opening the transaction at [lib.rs:8328](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:8328); that can mutate prior pending work, but not partially apply the rejecting request.

4. Legacy at-rest row: no data-availability defect found. `read_projections` loads legacy rows without applying the new validation; re-declaring only the valid half is destructive because removing an existing vector sub-object is destructive at [lib.rs:17329](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17329). The stated remedies, add `searchable` or drop, are accurate and tested in Rust at [slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:421](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:421). Rebuild/read paths operate from the stored registry and remain reachable.

5. Python/TS parity: rejection is covered; legacy behavior is not. See finding 1.

I did not run tests; this was a targeted read-only review, and several shell/git commands were blocked by the current sandbox.
